{"id": "EUVD-2026-103939", "enisaUuid": "352397af-8d57-36ad-86ad-6df8edcc5aed", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nsmb: client: discard post-EOF pagecache when extending a file via clone range\n\ncifs_remap_file_range() discarded the pagecache only for the folios\noverlapping the destination region, so when a clone extends the file the\nfolio straddling the old EOF - which may hold data dirtied past EOF\nthrough an mmap - was never dropped and became visible as file content\nonce the file was extended.\n\nStart the discard at the smaller of fstart and the old EOF.  i_size is\nstill old here, so nothing past the old EOF is flushed to the server.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:45:53", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:23:55", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/15bb9f1d3e967e328649e92a1451e60a0dc66118", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4721587f96cb8de8164f3fd203093a0875560999"], "aliases": ["GHSA-r85p-j355-crhr", "CVE-2026-98685"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.19, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "20b0e396-6dd5-324d-ada8-db7ef1838874", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.7"}, {"id": "2451f5d4-8df0-31ce-bdac-9cc9cba84510", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c54fc3a4f375663f2361a9cbb2955fb4ef912879 <15bb9f1d3e967e328649e92a1451e60a0dc66118"}, {"id": "32fd091d-9f9b-375c-91c6-9fcc984b3f3d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.1.68 <6.2"}, {"id": "6d17ab27-c380-3c28-88d8-324012034a4a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "358bd5f436d820bb758833050aae065b35d6986c"}, {"id": "91e9543f-292b-3cca-8e86-96d18accba4e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "ac284a16-5ce1-316a-b599-9123cdc042c7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": 